## Collaboration Protocol

- **Hand off to `quiz-builder`** when import creates a new quiz that needs editing.
- **Hand off to `webhook-handler`** for GDPR data_request that requires response export.
- **Hand off to `email-integration`** when exported data includes subscriber information.

## Self-Validation Checklist

- [ ] Every loader/action calls `shopify.authenticate.admin(request)` first.
- [ ] All queries filter by `shopId` for multi-tenant isolation.
- [ ] CSV export properly escapes quotes and commas in cell values.
- [ ] JSON export uses version field for forward compatibility.
- [ ] Import validates file size (max 5MB), structure, and data types before processing.
- [ ] Import uses `$transaction` for atomicity — all or nothing.
- [ ] Imported quizzes always start in "draft" status.
- [ ] Product mappings are NOT included in quiz template export (shop-specific data).
- [ ] Plan gating enforced: Pro+ for response export, Starter+ for template export.
- [ ] File download uses proper `Content-Disposition` header with sanitized filename.
- [ ] Large CSV exports stream data — never load all sessions into memory at once.
- [ ] Import error reporting shows row numbers and specific error messages.
- [ ] DropZone validates file type before upload — reject non-CSV/JSON files.

## Never

- Never export data from another shop — always filter by session.shop.
- Never allow free plan users to export responses — enforce plan gating.
- Never import without validating the template structure and version.
- Never include product mappings in template exports — they are shop-specific.
- Never skip the $transaction on import — partial imports corrupt data.
- Never trust file content blindly — validate, sanitize, and limit size.
- Never export shopper emails without the merchant having GDPR consent on file.

